WEBVTT

00:00:00.601 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:05.070
In the earlier lessons, we learned how to attach lashes:

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.830
classic, then volume.

00:00:07.329 --> 00:00:08.750
Today the question is:

00:00:08.831 --> 00:00:10.430
which lash goes where.

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:12.270
That is lash mapping.

00:00:12.669 --> 00:00:16.477
With the same pair of hands, but different lengths and curls,

00:00:16.427 --> 00:00:18.510
the eyes can look bigger, longer,

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:19.470
or sadder.

00:00:20.096 --> 00:00:23.309
Mapping means planning before you attach the first lash.

00:00:23.799 --> 00:00:28.681
We divide the lash line into a few zones, from the inner corner to the outer corner,

00:00:28.631 --> 00:00:30.349
and write down for each zone:

00:00:30.512 --> 00:00:33.149
how long the lashes are, and which curl.

00:00:33.558 --> 00:00:35.870
With a map, both eyes come out the same,

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:39.149
and the result is exactly what you agreed with the client.

00:00:39.491 --> 00:00:42.109
Without a map, the technician works by feel.

00:00:42.441 --> 00:00:43.789
And something that happens a lot:

00:00:44.131 --> 00:00:48.429
when you finish, the client sits up, and one eye looks longer than the other.

00:00:49.047 --> 00:00:52.045
Before choosing a style, you have to read the eyes.

00:00:52.581 --> 00:00:54.365
The first thing is the eye shape.

00:00:54.778 --> 00:00:55.805
Almond eyes:

00:00:55.906 --> 00:00:58.525
slightly long, and tapered at both ends.

00:00:58.863 --> 00:00:59.805
Round eyes:

00:00:59.913 --> 00:01:02.285
wide open, showing a lot of the iris.

00:01:02.622 --> 00:01:03.565
Hooded eyes:

00:01:03.673 --> 00:01:06.925
a fold of skin from the brow bone hangs down over the lid.

00:01:07.255 --> 00:01:08.445
And monolid eyes:

00:01:08.554 --> 00:01:10.525
a smooth lid, with no crease.

00:01:11.074 --> 00:01:12.846
Then downturned eyes:

00:01:13.097 --> 00:01:15.726
the outer corner sits lower than the inner corner.

00:01:16.131 --> 00:01:17.246
Upturned eyes:

00:01:17.515 --> 00:01:19.085
the outer corner sits higher.

00:01:19.589 --> 00:01:21.006
Eyes that are deep set:

00:01:21.288 --> 00:01:23.166
they sit deep under the brow bone.

00:01:23.513 --> 00:01:25.246
And the distance between the eyes:

00:01:25.435 --> 00:01:27.486
close together, or far apart.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:31.407
Look at the eye shape while the client is sitting up, eyes open,

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.606
looking straight ahead.

00:01:32.857 --> 00:01:37.646
Because once she is lying down with her eyes closed, all eyes look much the same.

00:01:38.235 --> 00:01:40.365
The second thing is the natural lashes.

00:01:40.697 --> 00:01:41.885
Long or short.

00:01:42.071 --> 00:01:43.405
Strong or fine.

00:01:43.754 --> 00:01:46.685
Growing downward, straight, or already curled.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.485
And are there sparse areas, or gaps?

00:01:50.046 --> 00:01:51.405
As in the classic lesson:

00:01:51.647 --> 00:01:55.725
an extension is never longer or heavier than the natural lash can carry.

00:01:56.072 --> 00:01:59.953
However beautiful the map, if the natural lashes cannot support it,

00:01:59.903 --> 00:02:00.925
it will not work.

00:02:01.499 --> 00:02:03.728
The third thing is what the client wants.

00:02:04.031 --> 00:02:05.648
Natural, or striking.

00:02:06.141 --> 00:02:08.848
Does she work in an office, or is she about to be a bride?

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:10.208
Does she wear glasses?

00:02:10.554 --> 00:02:14.288
Because lashes that are too long or too curled will touch the lenses.

00:02:14.786 --> 00:02:18.448
The eye shape, the natural lashes, and the client's wishes:

00:02:18.796 --> 00:02:20.768
these three together decide the map.

00:02:21.416 --> 00:02:22.865
Now the main styles.

00:02:23.013 --> 00:02:23.585
Remember:

00:02:23.774 --> 00:02:26.401
these are general tendencies, not hard rules,

00:02:26.351 --> 00:02:30.065
and every salon and every brand names them a little differently.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:33.105
The natural style follows the client's own lash line:

00:02:33.369 --> 00:02:36.796
short at the inner corner, a little longer toward the outer corner,

00:02:36.746 --> 00:02:39.265
and only slightly longer than the natural lashes.

00:02:39.661 --> 00:02:44.065
This style suits almost everyone, and it is a safe choice for a first time client.

00:02:44.726 --> 00:02:47.586
The doll style, also called open eye:

00:02:48.095 --> 00:02:52.095
the longest lashes sit in the middle of the eye, right above the pupil,

00:02:52.045 --> 00:02:53.986
then get shorter toward both ends.

00:02:54.406 --> 00:02:57.586
It makes the eyes look bigger, rounder and brighter.

00:02:58.016 --> 00:03:02.866
This style often suits almond eyes, small eyes, or downturned eyes.

00:03:03.215 --> 00:03:06.706
But on eyes that are already round, it can make them look too round.

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:08.960
The cat eye style is different:

00:03:09.146 --> 00:03:13.440
short at the inner corner, getting longer, and longest at the outer corner.

00:03:13.948 --> 00:03:17.440
It elongates the eyes, and gently lifts the outer corner.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:21.792
This style often suits round eyes, or eyes that are close together,

00:03:21.742 --> 00:03:23.680
because it draws the eyes outward.

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:26.800
The squirrel style sits between those two:

00:03:27.229 --> 00:03:30.279
the longest lashes are at about the outer third of the eye,

00:03:30.229 --> 00:03:32.720
then a little shorter right at the outer corner.

00:03:33.206 --> 00:03:36.480
The eye is lifted, without the outer corner being dragged down.

00:03:36.988 --> 00:03:38.000
And the fox eye:

00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:41.120
the inner and middle parts are fairly short and natural.

00:03:41.373 --> 00:03:44.580
Only the outermost part is longer, and usually more curled,

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.720
pointing up toward the tail of the brow.

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:50.160
The outer corner looks lifted, slim and sharp.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.334
Here is something that happens a lot.

00:03:52.835 --> 00:03:58.014
A client with downturned eyes sees a cat eye photo online, and wants exactly that.

00:03:58.414 --> 00:04:03.275
Do it, and the longest, heaviest lashes are concentrated at the outer corner,

00:04:03.225 --> 00:04:05.774
pulling the outer corner down even more.

00:04:06.193 --> 00:04:08.494
The eyes look more tired and sadder.

00:04:08.955 --> 00:04:10.124
With downturned eyes,

00:04:10.074 --> 00:04:14.014
you usually want to avoid putting the longest lashes at the outer corner.

00:04:14.261 --> 00:04:18.532
A doll style, or moving the longest point closer to the middle of the eye,

00:04:18.482 --> 00:04:20.414
with more curl on the outer part,

00:04:20.489 --> 00:04:21.694
will help lift the eye.

00:04:22.318 --> 00:04:24.350
Hooded eyes and monolid eyes:

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:27.070
the skin fold easily hides the lashes.

00:04:27.218 --> 00:04:31.310
So they usually need more curl, so the lashes rise above the fold and show.

00:04:31.875 --> 00:04:34.110
When the eyes are deep set, be careful:

00:04:34.421 --> 00:04:39.069
lashes that are too long or too curled may touch the upper lid, or the brow bone,

00:04:39.019 --> 00:04:40.830
when the client opens her eyes.

00:04:41.014 --> 00:04:42.806
And when the eyes are far apart,

00:04:42.756 --> 00:04:45.746
you usually emphasize the inner corner and the middle,

00:04:45.696 --> 00:04:47.870
rather than extending the outer corner.

00:04:48.195 --> 00:04:49.870
But these are only common patterns.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:52.990
Every client is different, and you have to see for yourself.

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:54.986
Now let's talk about curl.

00:04:55.567 --> 00:04:59.786
Lash extensions are named by letters, and the general idea is very simple:

00:05:00.125 --> 00:05:02.826
they go from nearly straight to strongly curled.

00:05:03.335 --> 00:05:06.666
J and B curls are nearly straight, for a natural look.

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:09.066
C is the most common curl.

00:05:09.569 --> 00:05:12.586
CC, and then D, are more curled:

00:05:12.935 --> 00:05:16.026
the lashes look more defined, and the eyes more open.

00:05:16.535 --> 00:05:19.706
And L has a straight base, and then bends upward.

00:05:20.047 --> 00:05:21.786
There are a few other types as well.

00:05:22.068 --> 00:05:24.340
Each brand curls a little differently,

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:28.026
so the same letter from two brands may not be exactly the same.

00:05:28.681 --> 00:05:32.606
How much curl to choose depends on the direction the natural lash grows.

00:05:32.975 --> 00:05:36.526
The base of the extension must lie flat along the natural lash.

00:05:37.032 --> 00:05:39.830
If the natural lash grows straight or downward,

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:43.806
and you attach a lash that is too curled, only a tiny point touches.

00:05:44.221 --> 00:05:47.486
It holds poorly, falls out early, and looks bent.

00:05:47.661 --> 00:05:52.565
For lashes that point down, some technicians choose a type with a straight base,

00:05:52.515 --> 00:05:56.206
like L, so the base hugs the natural lash and then curls up.

00:05:56.536 --> 00:05:57.505
On the other hand,

00:05:57.455 --> 00:06:01.486
if the natural lash is already curled and you attach one that is too straight,

00:06:01.755 --> 00:06:03.006
the extension sticks out.

00:06:03.594 --> 00:06:05.564
Two eyes are rarely identical.

00:06:05.814 --> 00:06:10.444
The natural lashes on one side may be longer, or sparser, than on the other.

00:06:10.948 --> 00:06:13.964
The map is not copied exactly from one eye to the other:

00:06:14.312 --> 00:06:15.935
the goal is a balanced result,

00:06:15.885 --> 00:06:18.924
so sometimes you adjust the lengths a little on one side.

00:06:19.353 --> 00:06:23.404
And before you start, show the client example photos, and be honest:

00:06:23.704 --> 00:06:27.724
which style suits these eyes, and how much her natural lashes can carry.

00:06:27.973 --> 00:06:30.204
Only once you both agree do you begin.

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:31.485
So you see.

00:06:31.914 --> 00:06:34.685
Mapping is not memorizing a few lash styles.

00:06:35.032 --> 00:06:39.832
It is looking at the eyes, looking at the natural lashes, listening to the client,

00:06:39.782 --> 00:06:41.165
and only then choosing.

00:06:41.673 --> 00:06:44.205
Once you understand, your hands will follow.

00:06:44.632 --> 00:06:48.445
In the practice lesson, we will draw a lash map, step by step.

00:06:48.866 --> 00:06:51.485
And now, take the short quiz below the video.

00:06:51.661 --> 00:06:52.525
See you next time.
